{{ ref: 37db2572-f788-819c-9ea8-e85e8b7a7a54 }}
## ⚠️ Constraints
--{ ref: 37db2572-f788-819c-9ea8-e85e8b7a7a54 }--

{{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8182-95d6-e17fa12dd8a7, is_toggleable: true }}
### C-1: Symbols Are Atomic
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-818e-8320-c14bc4bf15b9 }}
  **Constraint**: A symbol is never split. A single symbol exceeding the file cap is flagged `oversized symbol` and its file is exempted from the capacity violation.
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-818e-8320-c14bc4bf15b9 }--
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-818a-8aaf-f36ba2924f1a }}
  **Rationale**: Splitting symbol bodies is code rewriting — out of scope by FR-1.
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-818a-8aaf-f36ba2924f1a }--
--{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8182-95d6-e17fa12dd8a7 }--

{{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8105-a072-d30332c955ad, is_toggleable: true }}
### C-2: Exact Solving Bounded at 300 Nodes
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81ef-bba2-d43ca566f8bd }}
  **Constraint**: ILP-exact MFAS applies only to SCCs ≤ 300 nodes (configurable); larger SCCs use the Eades–Lin–Smyth heuristic with local search.
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81ef-bba2-d43ca566f8bd }--
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81a6-825a-f1922da100fe }}
  **Rationale**: MFAS is NP-hard; the bound keeps worst-case runtime predictable while covering virtually all real-world SCCs exactly.
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81a6-825a-f1922da100fe }--
--{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8105-a072-d30332c955ad }--

{{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8106-b0e9-e077704d7c1a }}
---
--{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8106-b0e9-e077704d7c1a }--

{{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8150-9105-d0dcfefce888 }}
## 💭 Assumptions
--{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8150-9105-d0dcfefce888 }--

{{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8135-94ad-fbcebe1e998a, is_toggleable: true }}
### A-1: Sources Are Well-Formed
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8173-a08e-fb9b946fd990 }}
  **Assumption**: Analyzed code parses and (for the Rust binder) resolves — the workspace builds.
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8173-a08e-fb9b946fd990 }--
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81f8-8a56-ecad30131c2e }}
  **Rationale**: Architecture analysis of unparseable code is undefined; failures surface as adapter errors, fast and early.
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81f8-8a56-ecad30131c2e }--
--{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8135-94ad-fbcebe1e998a }--

{{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81e8-9979-e50bd6c3e337, is_toggleable: true }}
### A-2: Consistent Formatting
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8158-97ae-fd57eb360a4f }}
  **Assumption**: Each repository applies a consistent formatter, keeping SLOC counts stable across commits.
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8158-97ae-fd57eb360a4f }--
  {{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8155-bf28-fd5d61dbf155 }}
  **Rationale**: The SLOC-based cap is formatter-sensitive; the ±10% borderline band absorbs residual churn.
  --{ ref: 37db2572-f788-8155-bf28-fd5d61dbf155 }--
--{ ref: 37db2572-f788-81e8-9979-e50bd6c3e337 }--

